    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0916" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg836"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 429.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 425, of
                    October 25 last, I inclose herewith for your information a copy of a note<anchor
                        n="d" xml:id="d796-f1"/> from the Danish minister stating that his
                    Government will issue a notice to Danish subjects in Salvador that they have
                    been placed under the protection of the United States as soon as it is informed
                    that the Salvadorean Government assents to such protection.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
